/-!
# The complement of an effective Cartier divisor on an algebraic space

Let `X` be an algebraic space over a scheme `S` contained in a big fppf site `B` and let
`D ⊆ X` be an effective Cartier divisor. Then the inclusion of the open complement `U = X ∖ D`
into `X` is an affine morphism, and `U` is scheme-theoretically dense in `X`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isLocallyPrincipal_of_isEffectiveCartierDivisor`: an effective
  Cartier divisor is a locally principal closed subspace.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isAffineHom_ι_openComplement_of_isEffectiveCartierDivisor`: the
  complementary open immersion is affine.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isSchemeTheoreticallyDense_openComplement_of_isEffectiveCartierDivisor`:
  the complement is scheme-theoretically dense.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank.isLocallyGeneratedByOnSite_one`: a
  sheaf of modules of rank one on a ringed site is locally generated by one section.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 083S](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/083S)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 083B](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/083B)
